description = "Experimental Xbox 360 core based on Xenia Edge. AMD GPUs default to the Vulkan backend (D3D12 is currently broken on AMD); others default to D3D12. Set the GPU Backend core option to Vulkan when running under Wine/Proton. GOD-format games launch via the extension-less package header file; disable 'Filter by supported extensions' to browse them."

notes = "No bundled system files are required; Xbox 360 games load directly.|(Controller) A standard Xbox 360/One pad maps 1:1 with no remapping needed.|(Controller) EmuVR forces input_player1_analog_dpad_mode = \"1\" on all cores, which doubles the left stick onto the d-pad for player 1. The bundled config/Xenia Edge/Xenia Edge.cfg pins it back off for this core; if you installed the core without that file, add input_player1_analog_dpad_mode = \"0\" (and player2..4) there yourself. A core has no API to change this - it is a frontend input setting.|(Optional, faster) Present via Vulkan: add video_driver = \"vulkan\" to that same config file. Not yet confirmed safe with the EmuVR VR view, so it ships commented out.|Keyboard analog-stick binds and the menu hotkey are global RetroArch settings, not core-settable."
